        {
          "id": "92dcc145-66ff-344f-99eb-9167a33f8b31",
          "content": {
            "id": "92dcc145-66ff-344f-99eb-9167a33f8b31",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Air France-KLM reports solid third-quarter results despite rising costs",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Air France-KLM reported solid third-quarter results Thursday (November 6) despite rising costs.</p><p>The airline also confirmed its outlook for this year even though it has seen higher expenses and costly challenges for KLM.</p><p>The group reported an operating profit of $1.40 billion - just below analyst forecasts but slightly higher than last year.</p><p>CEO Ben Smith said the carrier showed its resilience in a challenging environment during the period.</p><p>The group was particularly helped by lower fuel costs and solid bookings in its more luxurious premium cabins.</p><p>But it saw pressure on yields in its economy cabin with travel to the U.S.</p><p>European airlines have faced pressure as travel from Europe to the U.S. has dropped under President Donald Trump.</p><p>KLM was hit by lower yields in its economy cabin, as well as costly labor disputes in September.\u00a0</p><p>Air France-KLM shares were down 13% in early trade.</p><p>Investors were worried by the slight misalignment in expectations on the carrier's operating profit due to currency depreciation.</p><p>They also saw ongoing challenges with budget carrier Transavia and Dutch subsidiary KLM.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: Air France-KLM reported solid third-quarter results Thursday (November 6) despite rising costs.</p><p>The airline also confirmed its outlook for this year even though it has seen higher expenses and costly challenges for KLM.</p><p>The group reported an operating profit of $1.40 billion - just below analyst forecasts but slightly higher than last year.</p><p>CEO Ben Smith said the carrier showed its resilience in a challenging environment during the period.</p><p>The group was particularly helped by lower fuel costs and solid bookings in its more luxurious premium cabins.</p><p>But it saw pressure on yields in its economy cabin with travel to the U.S.</p><p>European airlines have faced pressure as travel from Europe to the U.S. has dropped under President Donald Trump.</p><p>KLM was hit by lower yields in its economy cabin, as well as costly labor disputes in September.&nbsp;</p><p>Air France-KLM shares were down 13% in early trade.</p><p>Investors were worried by the slight misalignment in expectations on the carrier's operating profit due to currency depreciation.</p><p>They also saw ongoing challenges with budget carrier Transavia and Dutch subsidiary KLM.</p></body>",
